      "isSatisfied": false,
      "text": "Generated test artifacts are written only to test-owned disposable output locations, not to repository fixture or documentation paths. The location is compared with the checkout by path segment under the path's own syntax: a Windows-form path (a drive letter or a backslash) ignores case, drive letter included, and a POSIX path compares ordinally; a case alias of the checkout or of a folder inside it is refused, and a distinct sibling is accepted (operator 2026-11-02: \"Strengthen 5 ACs, fix all 8 (Recommended)\"; hostile validation finding R9-F3). A path's root is part of its identity: a UNC path (two leading separators of either kind, then a server and a share) is in Windows form and compares its server, its share and its segments ignoring case, so a forward-slash, backslash or mixed-separator UNC alias of the checkout or of a folder inside it is refused, and a path under another root kind, server, share or drive letter is a different location (hostile validation round 10 finding R10-F2; strengthened between rounds under the operator's \"Strengthening Acceptance Criteria should always be the recommended option\" and \"don't gate on me between rounds\", 2026-11-03). That holds only within one path syntax: a folder is another location only when it and the checkout are both POSIX paths or both Windows paths (a drive letter or a UNC share), and a folder in the other syntax is refused, because on a POSIX host a path with two leading separators names the POSIX root and on Windows a single-rooted path names the current drive. A Windows device path (beginning \\\\?\\, \\\\.\\ or \\??\\, with either separator) and a Windows folder with a segment that ends in a dot or a space or holds a colon are refused too, because Windows resolves each to a location that may lie inside the checkout (findings of the hostile validation round 11 that stopped without a verdict, 2026-11-03; strengthened under the operator's \"Strengthening Acceptance Criteria should always be the recommended option\" and \"don't gate on me between rounds\"). The UNC server and share names are held to the same segment rule: a UNC folder whose server or share name ends in a dot or a space or holds a colon is refused, because Windows may resolve it to the checkout's server or share (holistic read before hostile validation round 12, finding D3; operator 2026-11-03: \"Strengthen + fix (Recommended)\")."
    },
