      "id": "ac-4",
      "isSatisfied": false,
      "text": "A test-owned temporary QBrain.AI instance uses the database inside its owned root: no inherited setting, in configuration or the process environment and in the canonical (QBrainAi, QBRAINAI_), legacy (Mcp, MCP_) or host-prefixed (DOTNET_, ASPNETCORE_) form, nor a connection-string or content-root variable, selects another database for it (a connection string, a data source, a database provider or an instance name), and a database selection outside the owned root is refused. Every consumer of a temporary instance takes its workspace, marker and server address from that instance, and no inherited setting overrides them. These are the unit-proved rules TR-MCP-NUKE-019 AC-6 relies on (operator 2026-10-29: \"Strengthen ACs, fix both (Recommended)\", \"Run the 2 classes, AC first (Recommended)\" and \"Lane ACs (Recommended)\"; operator 2026-10-30: \"FR-MCP-TESTRESOURCE-001 (Recommended)\"; hostile validation findings R8B-F2 and R8B-F3; holistic review findings PLAN-6, PLAN-7, RINT-1, RINT-2 and RINT-3). A REPL host started for a temporary instance names both a workspace and a marker, each strictly inside the instance's owned root, compared by path segment with either separator under the path's own syntax (a Windows-form path ignores case, drive letter included; a POSIX path compares ordinally; operator 2026-11-02: \"Strengthen 5 ACs, fix all 8 (Recommended)\", the sibling of hostile validation finding R9-F3) and with no '.' or '..' segment; the checkout's marker, another or sibling root, a parent-segment escape, the root itself as the marker, and a missing argument or value are refused (operator 2026-10-26: \"if you surface new AC, add them without waiting for approval\"; the start-argument rows of TemporaryInstanceChecksTests already prove it). Strict containment in the owned root also requires the same root: the same root kind (UNC, drive letter or POSIX) and the same root identity (server and share, or drive letter, compared ignoring case); a single-rooted path under a UNC owned root, a path on another server, share or drive, and a UNC path under a POSIX owned root are refused for the database, the workspace, the marker and the trust cache (hostile validation round 10 finding R10-F2; strengthened between rounds under the operator's \"Strengthening Acceptance Criteria should always be the recommended option\" and \"don't gate on me between rounds\", 2026-11-03). A setting is identified by its configuration key, not by its spelling: .NET configuration reads a process-environment name with a double underscore standing for the ':' delimiter and case ignored, and a DOTNET_ or ASPNETCORE_ prefix places the rest of the name in the host's configuration, so every colon, double-underscore or mixed-separator spelling of a key, alone or host-prefixed, sets that key. No inherited spelling of a product key or of the host's endpoint section (Kestrel), in either enumeration order of the inherited environment, changes the instance's effective database, workspace, marker or server address; unrelated variables are kept unchanged; and a start environment is refused before the instance starts when it holds a product key the instance did not set, under any spelling, or two names of one product key that differ only in separators or case (hostile validation round 12 finding R12-F1; strengthened between rounds under the operator's \"Strengthening Acceptance Criteria should always be the recommended option\" and \"don't gate on me between rounds\", 2026-11-05). A name is matched exactly, as the process environment holds it: two inherited names that differ only in case are two variables, and each unrelated one is kept with its own value. An inherited name that sets the same configuration key as one of the instance's own settings, under any spelling, is a competing value for that setting, not an unrelated variable: the instance's setting replaces it, and a start environment that holds two names of a key the instance sets that differ only in separators or case is refused, as two names of one product key are (seventh holistic read before hostile validation round 13, finding g1; strengthened between rounds under the operator's \"Strengthening Acceptance Criteria should always be the recommended option\" and \"don't gate on me between rounds\", 2026-11-05)."
