 B.9 HostileReview worker storage (section 16.7)\n"}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{"chunk_id":"608b05","wall_time_seconds":1.199223411,"exit_code":0,"original_token_count":6100,"output":"FILE docs/receipts/hv/hv-r4-store-REMED-HVPIPELINE-001.txt; lines=79\n1: type: result\n2: payload:\n3:   requestId: req-20261018T075741Z-d48e\n4:   result:\n5:     id: REMED-HVPIPELINE-001\n6:     title: Problems to fix found while preparing the durable multi-agent HV architecture amendment (pulled into the HV plan)\n7:     section: HostileValidation\n8:     priority: high\n9:     done: false\n10:     description:\n11:     - 'Single tracking item for every problem found while preparing the durable multi-agent hostile validation (HV) architecture amendment (operator, 2026-10-16T14:00 local, verbatim: \"keep track of problems to fix as a single todo item that will be pulled into the plan.\"). The HV plan PLAN-HVPIPELINE-001 pulls these items in (its last task; assignment in amendment section 20.4); nothing here is fixed by the documentation-only amendment, whose section 21 registers these problems (commits 31af8c597e3570a2469a48a238a4aa76107f30bb, 99cb42b24a442377a776aebd58e9df6894c2ce40, 9fd6b653b2522212ad8151091e3a8cdec25e75bd, 6dbc384323c036a57c37fd9eaf2259879c1d956f, bd6e37b33f043b1ede3a1feeaf7073d357ea21cf, f5fd5ab24ad00b09053daf07ed3c0d850f70498d, d3a0beb10b0879f20fb307f205a3bff25ac3a441, and 3fba1b1336a92767904e344dbe9d531200049a0d (hostile validation round 1 remediation: P1 corrected for finding F09, the P1 task for finding F18, and the P11 and P15 requirement corrected to FR-MCP-SESSIONLIFE-005), and 67297000747bcfacc481bc8891c35f8fe4aff65f (hostile validation round 2 remediation: P5 split into its foundation and HostileReview parts for finding R2-F04, the P1 worker contract completed for finding R2-F03, and the P7 named check), and 92df2c49d7f06f359190b8574dd5545d7174e294 (the completed pre-round-3 read: the P3 dispatch refusal with its diagnostic, the P1 host diagram matc