2933: ### 20.2 Gates
2934: 
2935: The foundation's gates apply unchanged (foundation section 8.4): G1 targeted tests, G2 the unit gate, G3 the integration suites with the three-provider cases, G4 the PowerShell plugin core, G5 configuration and traceability (strict), G6 the plugin suites, every one through Nuke, with zero failures and zero skips in the executed scope; the full unit suite of the current and earlier work passes before a context is left (AGENTS.md, "Byrd Test Gate"). The cases marked "three providers" in section 19 run in G3. The live check runs on a separate server instance started for it, never on a shared server (foundation section 8.6): it NONCEs every reviewer and records which pass and why (VI-01), submits a session-scope HV, watches the output stream receive lines while the reviewer runs (the end-to-end form of FR-MCP-HVPIPE-008-AC003), kills the worker mid-run and observes the lease recovery, cancels a second request, finalizes the first, reads its result and evidence, and confirms that writes to its turns are refused. Build, test, and deploy run through Nuke; releases through Octopus; GitHub Actions and Azure Pipelines are no part of any gate.
