der the owning plan's approved design and through its existing requirement, whose acceptance criteria H0 strengthens with a named test for the case the problem shows:\n2947: \n2948: - P10, P12, and P13 in HvStorageSchema, before any HV entity is created, because every HV entity is keyed by `WorkspaceId` first (section 12). P10 and P13 are fixed as the federation plan's P1.5 decided them: an explicit rekey maintenance command with its startup guard and the token-store key rewrite (its D5 and D7, `docs/plans/2026-10-07-federation-fixes.md:166-175`), never an automatic startup migration and never a dual-key lookup; P12 in the normalizer. Their requirements are FR, TR, and TEST-MCP-PATHNORM-001, which this workspace's store does not hold (requirement reads of 2026-10-17: `not_found`) and the federation handoff places in the `F:\\GitHub\\McpServer` store (`docs/handoffs/federation-fixes-handoff-20261016T121400.md:97`); H0 imports them into this workspace's store through the requirements workflow, with their stored text, before strengthening them.\n2949: - P11, P14, and P15 in H1, in the PowerShell plugin core and synced to every plugin that carries it, before FR-MCP-HVPIPE-008-AC010 (a reviewer closes its own turn and exits under the Stop gate) is bound to the real hosts: P11 and P15 break the Stop path that criterion runs through, and P14 is in the REPL wrapper that every hook call runs through (`plugins/core/lib-ps/plugin-hook.ps1:230`, `plugins/core/lib-ps/repl-invoke.ps1:771,959`). P11 and P15 follow the foundation's stop gate, which blocks while a delivered request is in progress and never closes a turn (its FR-MCP-SESSIONTURN-005, slice A7), never Codex's suggestion to complete the turn in the hook. Their requirement in the store is FR-MCP-SESSIONLIFE-005: P11 is its criterion 2 (a stale local turn is reconciled only by authoritative `Completed` proof for the exact workspace, agent, session, and request) and P15 its criterion 1 (failed-build and incomplete-audit enforcement before any allow), although the hook cites FR-MCP-SESSIONLIFE-004 for both (`plugins/core/lib-ps/plugin-hook.ps1:972,1044`), a citation H1 corrects with the fix, as P7 corrects `EventStreamController`'s (requirement reads of 2026-10-17). P14's is FR-MCP-SESSIONLIFE-004 criterion 1.\n2950: - Named tests, H0 against mocks and bound in the phase that fixes each problem, recorded on the TEST of the requirement named: `WorkspaceRekeyRewritesStoredBackslashKeysThreeProviders` and `StartupGuardRefusesUnconvertedWorkspaceKeys` (P10), `CombineResolvesRootRelativeWindowsSegmentAgainstDrive` (P12), and `RekeyRewritesGitHubTokenEntriesReadUpdateDelete` (P13), on TEST-MCP-PATHNORM-001; `StopHookStaleCacheReconciledByExactTurnCompletedProof` (P11), `StopOverrideMarkerNeverPassesInProgressTurn` (P15), and `ReplChildTreeKillsDescendantsAfterRootExit` (P14) on TEST-MCP-SESSIONLIFE-002, the TEST that both FR-MCP-SESSIONLIFE-004 and -005 map to and that holds their child-deadline, cleanup, Stop-ordering, and stop-hook pin tests (its criterion 2; store reads of 2026-10-17: TEST-MCP-SESSIONLIFE-005 belongs to the drain-timeout work of FR-MCP-REPL-011).\n2951: - Where an owning plan has already delivered the same fix under its approved design when the phase starts, the phase proves it with the named test and does not change that code a second time (the DRY ruling).\n2952: \n2953: ### 20.5 Verification items (H0 and H1)\n2954: \n2955: Each item states what it asks and, where the drafting session settled it, the result of 2026-10-16 with its receipt. The probe runs ran each CLI headless in an empty scratch directory outside every workspace, each bounded by a timeout (probes, not hostile validations), and their complete outputs are kept under `/home/sharpninja/.claude/receipts/McpServer/20261016T153600-hv-amendment-vi-probes/`. What stays open is verified in H1 or H0 as stated.\n2956: \n2957: - VI-01 For each of the five CLIs, the runtime receipt that names the model and effort of