and the bytes stored, the ledger rows included, each chunk's ledger row carrying its own compressed copy of the chunk (R-14). Open for H1: the measurement.\n2962: - VI-06 The column or ordinal that gives a session's turn order. Settled: develop has no ordinal column on `SessionLogTurnEntity` and reads a session's turns by ascending row `Id` (`src/QBrainAi.Services/Services/SessionLogService.cs:504,693,2002`; `src/QBrainAi.Support.Mcp/Services/TransactionGatedSessionLogService.cs:445,476,694`); one federation adapter orders by `Timestamp` instead (`src/QBrainAi.Services/Services/FederationAdapters/FederationStateAdapterImplementations.cs:1063`), which HvScopeResolution does not use.\n2963: - VI-07 That a multi-member response log reads back as one stream. Settled on .NET 10.0.13: one `GZipStream` over three concatenated members returned the exact concatenation (305136 bytes, equal SHA-256), and the first member alone did not (negative control); FR-MCP-HVPIPE-011-AC004 repeats the check on the server's runtime.\n2964: - VI-08 The highest effort each CLI accepts. Settled: Codex `max` (accepted and recorded in its rollout), Claude `max` (recorded in its transcript), Grok `xhigh` (Grok 1.0.60 refuses `max` and lists `xhigh`, `high`, `medium`, `low`), Cline `xhigh` (its `--thinking` levels end at `xhigh`), Copilot `max` (its `--reasoning-effort` values, subject to the configured model); section 10 holds the table, and P9 records where develop's constants differ.\n2965: \n2966: ## 21. Problem register (REMED-HVPIPELINE-001)\n2967: \n2968: The single TODO of problems to fix found while writing this amendment (operator, 2026-10-16: \"keep track of problems to fix as a single todo item that will be pulled into the plan.\"), created and read back through the plugin on 2026-10-16; P10 to P15, the six findings of the Codex review of pull request 81 (review 5554472359 on commit `6dbc384323`, posted 2026-10-16T17:48:12 local, after the merge), were added on 2026-10-17 at the operator's answer \"1. Yes\", each checked against the source of this branch. Each item's full text and receipts are in the TODO; summaries:\n2969: \n2970: - P1 Requirement drift and a missing worker: the exported projection `docs/Project/Functional-Requirements.md:1389` shows FR-MCP-HOSTILEREVIEW-003 acceptance criterion 4 (a server-owned leased worker) checked with an older text, while the store holds it with `isSatisfied` false and a newer text (the configured or the pooled default agent, no named model; requirement read of 2026-10-17); either way no worker exists: none is registered and `AcceptReviewerOutputAsync` has no caller in `src` (`HostileReviewServiceCollectionExtensions.cs:11-42`; lease options unread, `HostileReviewWorkerOptions.cs:30-46`).\n2971: - P2 Defect: `AcceptReviewerOutputAsync` overwrites the verdict on every call with no lease, attempt, or fence (`HostileReviewService.cs:196-273`).\n2972: - P3 Requirement drift: FR-MCP-HOSTILEREVIEW-002 lists many artifact types, but only `todo` resolves, and the stored hash is of the TODO id, not its content (`HostileReviewService.cs:294-314`).\n2973: - P4 Audit gap: the ledger is skipped when the audit table is unavailable, and entities without `IsDeleted` are never audited (`McpDbContext.cs:1507-1538,1620-1627`).\n2974: - P5 Reviewer pin drift: the foundation pins one grader and model, contrary to P-01 and S-02 (A-01 to A-03), and `HostileReviewWorkerOptions.Validate` pins `Astra`, `gpt-6-astra`, and `xhigh` (`HostileReviewWorkerOptions.cs:77-82`), contrary to FR-MCP-HOSTILEREVIEW-003 criterion 4 (the configured or the pooled default agent, no named model); the two parts are fixed in H0 and H3 (section 20.4).\n2975: - P6 Capability gap: the one-shot strategy has no Copilot branch; Copilot runs only through the interactive `copilot-cli` strategy, unqualified for HV (`OneShotCliAgentExecutionStrategy.cs:238-262`, `CopilotCliAgentExecutionStrategy.cs:5-45`).\n2976: - P7 Traceability drift: `EventStreamController`