xed in it (section 20.4). Sources: FR-MCP-HOSTILEREVIEW-002 (it reviews artifacts) against S-03 (this pipeline reviews session turns); the approved foundation's position (foundation section 5.4); the operator rule that new scope the operator has not named needs approval, which consolidation would be. Its missing worker has its own contract (section 16.7) and shares only the compatible execution primitives (the DRY ruling).\n2992: - D-03 (open, the operator's) The foundation amendments A-01 to A-12, with this amendment and its plan: approve them as a change to PLAN-SESSIONTURNREVIEW-001, which then needs its new hostile validation (section 1). The operator's rules make plan approval the operator's act: a requirement change is planned, presented, and implemented only after explicit approval.\n2993: - D-04 (settled by the operator, 2026-10-17) The reviewer for the hostile validation of this amendment and its plan is Codex `gpt-6-astra` at effort `max`. Source: the operator's answer \"2. A\" to the question asked under P-01 (\"If not specified by operator, ask what agent and model to use for HV in a session.\"). Codex is neither the requesting agent's family (ClaudeCode) nor the agent that drafted the first version (Cline); its model and effort are verified from its rollout (VI-01).\n2994: - D-05 (settled) Exclusion covers the author of the reviewed turns as well as the submitter (R-08, FR-MCP-HVPIPE-002-AC008). Sources: S-28 (a self-review \"is not relevant to the HV\"), P-07 (\"Self-check alone is not validation.\"), and the handoff's settled requirement that self-review is independent of HV; a review by the agent that wrote the turns is a self-review. Because one request names turns of one MCP session (R-26), the author is that session's agent.\n2995: - D-06 (settled) Cline stays unqualified until it records the effort of a run: its NONCE fails `runtime_identity_mismatch` (L-04). Sources: P-04 (\"Verify the reviewer's model and effort from its own runtime receipts\"), which leaves no accepted remedy for a declared, unobserved effort; the operator rule to fail closed under an existing rule when the inputs cannot prove a fact; the handoff's settled requirement that not every request needs all five reviewers. The same holds for the HostileReview worker of section 16.7, whose execution row records the model and effort actually used (FR-MCP-HOSTILEREVIEW-003 criteria 1 and 2): an agent without a provenance source fails its attempt with `runtime_identity_unavailable` before launch.\n2996: - D-07 (settled by the operator, 2026-10-17) This plan fixes P10 to P15 itself, in HvStorageSchema and H1, each under the owning plan's approved design (the federation plan's D5 and D7; the foundation's FR-MCP-SESSIONTURN-005), as section 20.4 assigns them (operator, verbatim: \"D-07 B: this plan fixes all six (P10 to P15) itself.\"). The question arose because each sits in code another plan owns or has redesigned: P10 and P13 are the federation plan's undelivered P1.5, P12 is in that plan's normalizer code, P11 and P15 are in the stop path the foundation's slice A7 rewrites, and P14 is under FR-MCP-SESSIONLIFE-004, which the foundation lists as related and unchanged. Rejected: option A, which left each fix to its owning plan with this plan holding only entry conditions.\n2997: - D-08 (settled by the operator, 2026-10-17) Timestamps in HV data: the identifiers `hvr-`, `hvprobe-`, and `hvi-` keep the UTC `yyyyMMddTHHmmssZ` stamp, as session and request ids do, and every stored timestamp is UTC with offset (section 12); local time is for display only (operator, verbatim: \"HV ids keep the UTC yyyyMMddTHHmmssZ stamp: timestamps are UTC in the data and local only for display.\"). The question arose because the operator profile's rule of 2026-10-13 (\"Local everywhere\") asks that a UTC identifier be raised to the operator.\n2998: - D-09 (settled by the operator, 2026-10-17) The existing requirement records through which the problems of section 21 are fixed (TEST-MCP-HOSTILEREVIEW-002 and -003, FR-MCP-SESSIONLIFE-004 and -005, TEST-MCP-SESSIONLIFE-002, and the import of FR, TR, and TEST-MCP-PATHNORM-001; section 19.3) change in H0, after the operator approves the plan, and not before (operator, verbatim: \"B\", choosing option B of the question asked that day). The question arose because the workspace rule to capture requirements as they emerge argued for changing them at once, while FR-MCP-HOSTILEREVIEW-003 criterion 4 cites PLAN-SESSIONTRIAGEFIX-001, which the operator paused on 2026-10-16, so a change now could resume that plan. Until H0, the strengthened criteria and their named tests are stated in sections 16.7 and 20.4 and in REMED-HVPIPELINE-001. Rejected: option A, which updated those records in the store before hostile validation round 2.\n2999: \n3000: ## 23. Diagram index\n3001: \n3002: - Section 4: the system context.\n3003: - Section 7: the state diagrams of the HV request (7.1), the run attempt (7.2), reviewer readiness (7.3), and a turn's HV state (7.4).\n3004: - Section 11, the shared components, each drawn once: FencedLease, GzipCodec, AuditLedgerGuard, AgentIdentity, TurnSnapshotBuilder, RequirementReferenceExtractor, NotificationOutbox, OrderedEventReplay.\n3005: - Section 14, units of work: ListHvReviewersQuery, GetHvReviewerQuery, UpdateHvReviewerCommand, StartHvReviewerNonceCommand; SubmitHvRequestCommand (nested activities AdmitRequestChecks and InsertAdmittedRequest), GetHvRequestQuery, QueryHvRequestsQuery, CancelHvRequestCommand; GetHvResultQuery, GetHvEvidenceQuery, RemoveHvEvidenceCommand, StreamHvRunOutputQuery, StreamHvNotificationsQuery, QueryHvNotificationsQuery, QueryHvIncidentsQuery; ClaimHvRunCommand, RecordHvRunStartCommand, RecordHvRunHeartbeatCommand, AppendHvRunOutputCommand, CloseHvRunOutputCommand, FailHvRunCommand, ExpireHvRunLeasesCommand, FinalizeHvRequestCommand (nested activities ReadFinalizationInputs and CommitFinalResult), FileHvIncidentCommand; section 14.5, the amended internal RecordModelGradeCommand.\n3006: - Section 15, policies: HvScopeResolution, HvAdmissionEligibility, HvReviewerEligibility, RoundRobinAssignment, HvTurnFreeze, HvFinalVerification (nested activities VerifyLogAndBinding and VerifyVerdictAndReviewer), ReadinessProbeVerdict, HvProbeOutcome, HvRetryDecision.\n3007: - Section 16, processes: HvWorkerHost, RunReviewerProcess (nested activities StreamReviewerOutput and FailAttempt), SubmitHvFromPlugin, WatchHvNotifications, and HostileReviewWorkerHost (nested activity RunHostileReviewAttempt) with its internal units ClaimHostileReviewAttemptCommand, RenewHostileReviewAttemptCommand, CompleteHostileReviewAttemptCommand, and ExpireHostileReviewLeasesCommand (section 16.7).\n3008: - Section 17, sequences: 17.1 to 17.15, with the nested sequences StreamOneAttempt and FinalizeOneRequest after 17.7.\n3009: - Section 18, use cases: the overview and UC-HV-01 to UC-HV-12.\n3010: - Section 20: the delivery order.\n3011: - Addendum B, entity diagrams by functionality: B.1 references between the groups, B.2 reviewer pool, B.3 requests and membership, B.4 runs and output, B.5 results and findings, B.6 evidence, B.7 notifications and incidents, B.8 changed foundation entities, B.9 HostileReview worker storage.\n3012: \n3013: ## Addendum B. Entity diagrams with relationships\n3014: \n3015: Grouped by functionality, the foundation's rule (Addendum A, \"Grouping\"): each entity's columns appear in exactly one group; an entity of another group appears without columns only as a relationship target. Solid lines are database foreign keys (each the composite (`WorkspaceId`, parent key)); dotted lines are logical references by root ids, enforced by the units. Diagrams draw key columns and the columns this amendment adds; section 12 lists every column of the HV entities, and section 16.7 those of the HostileReview worker (B.9, whose single-column foreign keys are that subsystem's own).\n3016: \n3017: ### B.1 References between the groups\n3018: \n3019: - An HV request names its reviewed session by `Agent` and `SessionId`, its submitting turn by the submitter turn key, and each member turn by its turn key; a run names the reviewer's own turn by `ReviewerAgent`, `ReviewerSessionId`, and `ReviewerRequestId`; a requirement reference names a requirement or use case by `RefId`; an incident names its triage report by `TriageReportId`.\n3020: \n3021: ```mermaid\n3022: erDiagram\n3023:     SessionLog ||..o{ HvRequest : \"reviewed session, by Agent and SessionId\"\n3024:     SessionLogTurn ||..o{ HvRequest : \"submitting turn key\"\n3025:     SessionLogTurn ||..o{ HvRequestTurn : \"member turn key\"\n3026:     SessionLogTurn ||..o{ HvRun : \"reviewer turn key\"\n3027:     Requirement ||..o{ HvRequestRequirementRef : \"RefId\"\n3028:     TriageReport ||..o{ HvIncident : \"TriageReportId\"\n3029:     HvReviewer ||..o{ HvRequest : \"AssignedReviewerId\"\n3030:     HvReviewer ||..o{ HvRun : \"ReviewerId\"\n3031: ```\n3032: \n3033: ### B.2 Reviewer pool\n3034: \n3035: Not drawn: `HvReviewer` `ConfigurationVersion`, `ExecutionStrategy`, `AgentPath`, `ConfiguredModel`, `ConfiguredEffort`, `ResolvedModel`, `ResolvedEffort`, `ReadinessReason`, `ReadinessChangedUtc`, `LastProbeRunId`, `OpenIncidentId`, `ProbeRequestedUtc`, `MaxConcurrentRuns`, `CreatedUtc`, `UpdatedUtc`.\n3036: \n3037: ```mermaid\n3038: erDiagram\n3039:     HvWorkspaceState {\n3040:         string WorkspaceId PK\n3041:         string LastAssignedReviewerId\n3042:         long NextNotificationSequence\n3043:         int StateVersion\n3044:     }\n3045:     HvReviewer {\n3046:         string WorkspaceId PK\n3047:         string ReviewerId PK\n3048:         bool Enabled\n3049:         string Readiness\n3050:         int StateVersion\n3051:     }\n3052:     HvWorkspaceState ||..o{ HvReviewer : \"same workspace, cursor names a reviewer\"\n3053: ```\n3054: \n3055: ### B.3 Requests and membership\n3056: \n3057: Not drawn: `HvRequest` scope, submitter, context, state, and result columns of section 12; unique (`WorkspaceId`, `IdempotencyKey`); indexes (`WorkspaceId`, `Status`, `CreatedUtc`) and (`WorkspaceId`, `Agent`, `SessionId`). `HvRequestTurn`: unique (`WorkspaceId`, `HvRequestId`, `Ordinal`) and the unique filtered turn-key index where `Disposition` is `Pending`. `HvRequestResponse`: unique (`WorkspaceId`, `HvRequestId`, `ResponseId`) and unique filtered (`WorkspaceId`, `ResponseId`) where `Disposition` is `Pending`.\n"}}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{"i":1,"status":"fulfilled","value":{"chunk_id":"b51a45","wall_time_seconds":1.163652256,"exit_code":0,"original_token_count":1080,"output":"FILE docs/architecture/SessionTurn-Review-AgentContext-Architecture-Amendment-1-Durable-HV.md; lines=3286\n3058: \n3059: ```mermaid\n3060: erDiagram\n3061:     HvRequest {\n3062:         string WorkspaceId PK\n3063:         string HvRequestId PK\n3064:         string ScopeKind\n3065:         string Agent\n3066:         string SessionId\n3067:         string IdempotencyKey UK\n3068:         string Status\n3069:         string AssignedReviewerId\n3070:         int AttemptCount\n3071:         string OverallVerdict\n3072:     }\n3073:     HvRequestTurn {\n3074:         long Id PK\n3075:         string HvRequestId FK, UK\n3076:         int Ordinal UK\n3077:         string Agent UK\n3078:         string SessionId UK\n3079:         string RequestId UK\n3080:         string SnapshotSha256\n3081:         string Disposition\n3082:     }\n3083:     HvRequestRequirementRef {\n3084:         long Id PK\n3085:         string HvRequestId FK, UK\n3086:         int Ordinal UK\n3087:         string Kind\n3088:         string RefId\n3089:         bool Resolved\n3090:     }\n3091:     HvRequestResponse {\n3092:         long Id PK\n3093:         string HvRequestId FK, UK\n3094:         string ResponseId FK, UK\n3095:         string Disposition\n3096:         string GradeId\n3097:     }\n3098:     AgentResponse {\n3099:         string ResponseId PK\n3100:     }\n3101:     HvRequest ||--o{ HvRequestTurn : \"members\"\n3102:     HvRequest ||--o{ HvRequestRequirementRef : \"references\"\n3103:     HvRequest ||--o{ HvRequestResponse : \"linked responses\"\n3104:     AgentResponse ||--o{ HvRequestResponse : \"graded in\"\n3105: ```\n3106: \n3107: ### B.4 Runs and output\n3108: \n3109: Not drawn: `HvRun` timestamps, `ReviewerConfigurationVersion`, `ProcessId`, `ExitCode`, `FailureDetail`, `ExpectedModel`, `ExpectedEffort`, `ProbeNonce`, the output manifest, progress, and provenance columns of section 12; the unique filtered (`WorkspaceId`, `HvRequestId`) where `Status` is live. `HvRunOutputChunk`: unique (`WorkspaceId`, `RunId`, `Sequence`); `LineCount`, `ByteCount`, `FenceToken`, `CreatedUtc`, `RemovedUtc`.\n3110: \n3111: ```mermaid\n3112: erDiagram\n3113:     HvRun {\n3114:         string WorkspaceId PK\n3115:         string RunId PK\n3116:         string Kind\n3117:         string HvRequestId FK, UK\n3118:         string ReviewerId\n3119:         int Attempt\n3120:         string LeaseOwner\n3121:         long FenceToken\n3122:         string Status\n3123:         string ReviewerSessionId\n3124:         string ReviewerRequestId\n3125:     }\n3126:     HvRunOutputChunk {\n3127:         long Id PK\n3128:         string RunId FK, UK\n3129:         int Sequence UK\n3130:         bytes Payload\n3131:         string Sha256\n3132:         string ChainSha256\n3133:     }\n3134:     HvRequest {\n3135:         string HvRequestId PK\n3136:     }\n3137:     HvRequest |o--o{ HvRun : \"attempts, null for a probe\"\n3138:     HvRun ||--o{ HvRunOutputChunk : \"ordered output\"\n3139: ```\n3140: \n3141: ### B.5 Results and findings\n3142: \n3143: Not drawn: `HvTurnAssessment` `Summary`, `RunId`; `HvFinding` `ResponseId`, `Check`, `Location`, `RequirementRef`, `ClaimId`, `Evidence`, `Remediation`, `RunId`; each unique with (`WorkspaceId`, `HvRequestId`, `Ordinal`).\n3144: \n3145: ```mermaid\n3146: erDiagram\n3147:     HvTurnAssessment {\n3148:         long Id PK\n3149:         string HvRequestId FK, UK\n3150:         int Ordinal UK\n3151:         string RequestId\n3152:         decimal Correctness\n3153:         decimal Completeness\n3154:         string Verdict\n3155:         string MappedReviewStatus\n3156:     }\n3157:     HvFinding {\n3158:         long Id PK\n3159:         string HvRequestId FK, UK\n3160:         int Ordinal UK\n3161:         string Scope\n3162:         int TurnOrdinal\n3163:         string Outcome\n3164:         string Category\n3165:     }\n3166:     HvRequest {\n3167:         string HvRequestId PK\n3168:     }\n3169:     HvRequest ||--o{ HvTurnAssessment : \"per-turn assessments\"\n3170:     HvRequest ||--o{ HvFinding : \"failures\"\n3171: ```\n3172: \n3173: ### B.6 Evidence\n3174: \n3175: Not drawn: `ByteCount`, `CompressedBytes`, `ContentType`, `CreatedUtc`, `RemovedBy`, `RemovalReason`; unique (`WorkspaceId`, `HvRequestId`, `Kind`).\n3176: \n3177: ```mermaid\n3178: erDiagram\n3179:     HvEvidence {\n3180:         long Id PK\n3181:         string HvRequestId FK, UK\n3182:         string Kind UK\n"}}"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a14dff-3460-7c42-bc45-42dc952fc93c","create_time":1792310656.2369516}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
