1: [{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sharpninja/McpServer/pulls/comments/4300020822","pull_request_review_id":5554472359,"id":4300020822,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDORUA_QM8AAAABAE0cVg","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,80 @@\n+using Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore;\n+using Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore.ChangeTracking;\n+using Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore.Storage.ValueConversion;\n+\n+namespace QBrainAi.Support.Mcp.Storage;\n+\n+/// <summary>\n+/// FR-MCP-PATHNORM-001 / TR-MCP-PATHNORM-001: persisted workspace keys (every <c>WorkspaceId</c>,\n+/// <c>OwnerWorkspaceId</c> and entity <c>WorkspacePath</c> column) are stored in the lexical canonical\n+/// form from <see cref=\"WorkspaceIdentity.CanonicalizeWorkspaceId\"/>. The converter applies on writes\n+/// and, on relational providers, to query parameters compared with these properties, so a predicate\n+/// built from a caller's raw path (<c>Q:\\ws</c>) matches the stored canonical row (<c>Q:/ws</c>). The\n+/// comparer makes the change tracker treat both spellings as one key.\n+/// </summary>\n+internal static class WorkspaceKeyConversion\n+{\n+    private static readonly HashSet<string> PropertyNames = new(StringComparer.Ordinal)\n+    {\n+        \"WorkspaceId\",\n+        \"OwnerWorkspaceId\",\n+        \"WorkspacePath\",\n+    };\n+\n+    private static readonly ValueConverter<string, string> Converter = new(\n+        value => WorkspaceIdentity.CanonicalizeWorkspaceId(value),\n+        value => value);","path":"src/QBrainAi.Storage/WorkspaceKeyConversion.cs","commit_id":"6dbc384323c036a57c37fd9eaf2259879c1d956f","original_commit_id":"6dbc384323c036a57c37fd9eaf2259879c1d956f","user":{"login":"chatgpt-codex-connector[bot]","id":199175422,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOC98s_g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/1144995?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/chatgpt-codex-connector%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/chatgpt-codex-connector","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chatgpt-codex-connector%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chatgpt-codex-connector%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chatgpt-codex-connector%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chatgpt-codex-connector%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chatgpt-codex-connector%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chatgpt-codex-connector%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chatgpt-codex-connector%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chatgpt-codex-connector%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chatgpt-codex-connector%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Migrate legacy workspace keys before canonical queries**\n\nOn an upgraded Windows installation, existing rows contain the previous `Q:\\workspace` spelling, while this converter canonicalizes new writes and query parameters to `Q:/workspace` but leaves values read from storage unchanged. Because this commit includes no data migration, SQLite/PostgreSQL comparisons against the canonical discriminator no longer match those legacy rows, so tenant-filtered data becomes invisible and workspace bootstrap can create parallel rows. Add a provider migration that rewrites every affected key and foreign key before enabling this converter.\n\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\n\n<!-- codex-code-review-finding:v1 -->","created_at":"2026-10-16T22:48:12Z","updated_at":"2026-10-16T22:48:13Z","html_url":"https://github.com/sharpninja/McpServer/pull/81#discussion_r4300020822","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sharpninja/McpServer/pulls/81","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/sharpninja/McpServer/pulls/comments/4300020822"